    "body": "> It looks like `PROMPT_COMMAND` might be defined as `readonly` in the global `/etc/bashrc` file. Please try removing the line that sets the `PROMPT_COMMAND` variable as read-only, though this might have an impact on system upgrades.\r\n\r\nThanks, according to your guide, I found the global bash config file on my host (`etc/bash.bashrc`),It actually does have a line about the `PROMPT_COMMAND` variable setting.\r\nBut unfortunately I don't have permission to edit this file, because the host is provided by my company,and IT guy didn't assign me sudo privileges.\r\nAnyway, thanks for your help!",
